Original commit body from f091b9a:

The UsageContext infrastructure (ADR-0003 v1.1.x) was implemented in
individual analyzers but never connected to the output pipeline:

- collect_analyzer_result() wasn't collecting result.usage_contexts
- run_all_analyzers() wasn't returning usage_contexts
- enrich_symbols() wasn't being passed usage_contexts
- behavior_map JSON output didn't include usage_contexts field

This fix completes the wiring:

1. all_analyzers.py: Add all_usage_contexts parameter to
   collect_analyzer_result() and include in run_all_analyzers() return

2. cli.py: Capture all_usage_contexts from run_all_analyzers(),
   pass to enrich_symbols(), and add to behavior_map output

3. schema.py: Add usage_contexts to new_behavior_map() factory

Analyzers that emit usage_contexts (Python, JS/TS, Go, Ruby, Elixir,
Rust) will now have their call-based framework patterns (Django URLs,
Express routes, etc.) appear in the JSON output.
